silm:instances_papers_02_music_sections_02_twelve_gaps_yoneda_hom_leg silm:hasExample "In '02TwelvegapsYonedaHomLeg', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, In the Music graph engine entry section 02_twelve_gaps, the '] tikzcd% The twelve-gap closure diagram: gaps G1--G12 are closed when the source packet can be typed (G1), claimed as a typed arrow (G2), assigned a dependency (G3), manifested (G4), validated (G5), traced (G6), serialized (G7), ungated-shortcut-free (G8), catus-collision-free (G9), citation-bounded (G10), storage-coherent (G11), and Yoneda-closed (G12).fig:music-gaps-closure Diagram law (Figure~fig:music-gaps-closure): the gap-closure diagram commutes when every numbered gap is sealed; a missing node or arrow in the diagram signals an unclosed gap in the page's construction obligation. [0.88]% tikzcd[column sep=large,row sep=large,ampersand replacement=\\&] G9:CatusCollision [r,dashed, arrow witnesses the Mittens microchip-id arrow witnessing identifier-by-leg, distinct from identifier-as-Mittens.; also, In the Music graph engine entry section 02_twelve_gaps, the ] [ur, arrow witnesses the DomesticCat classification arrow as a typed source leg into D_Mittens — NOT an identity onto Mittens." .
